      <Ordine>25</Ordine>
      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission oil filter replacement procedure</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;LI&gt; The gearbox oil filter should be replaced when: &lt;BR/&gt;
&lt;LI&gt; The car has reached 60,000 km &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Coolant has contaminated the gearbox oil &lt;BR/&gt;    &lt;LI&gt; Metal particles have been found in the gearbox oil &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; The clutch is worn or malfunctioning &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Move the gear lever to &lt;B&gt; P &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Remove the automatic gearbox oil filter cover &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt; CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt; Cover the area around the filter with cloths &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Loosen the automatic gearbox oil filter screw by &lt;B&gt; 7 turns &lt;/B&gt;  &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Wait 10 seconds to allow the oil in the filter to drain into the gearbox housing &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Remove the automatic gearbox filter &lt;B&gt; (A) &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Proceed with replacing the filter &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Refitting the automatic gearbox filter cover &lt;B&gt; (A) &lt;/B&gt; and tightening it to &lt;B&gt; 20 Nm &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt; CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt; Always replace the automatic gearbox filter gasket</Corpo>
