      <Ordine>30</Ordine>
      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission oil level check</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;html xmlns:v=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml&quot; xmlns:o=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; xmlns:w=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word&quot; xmlns:m=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2004/12/omml&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40&quot;&gt;     &lt;body lang=IT style=&apos;tab-interval:35.4pt&apos;&gt;  &lt;div class=WordSection1&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the vehicle on a level&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Lift the vehicle&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Remove the bottom cover&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Connect the diagnostic tester&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Make sure that the temperature of the gearbox oil is between &lt;B&gt;35~ 45 °C.&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Via diagnostio tester, start the &lt;B&gt;automatic transmission oil level check &lt;/B&gt;procedure&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Start the engine at idle&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the shift lever in &lt;B&gt;P&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the waste oil collection tray under the vehicle. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Remove the level verification cap &lt;B&gt;B&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Allow excess oil to drain away.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Check the oil level of the automatic transmission.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; The right amount is confirmed by a slight drip&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; If oil is not dripping from the inspection hole, it will be necessary to add another liter of oil using the &lt;B&gt;VAS 6262A &lt;/B&gt;adapter&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; If the oil turns out to be in excess, it will be necessary to allow it to drain off until a slight drip is obtained&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt;If it is necessary to add oil, shake the bottles well before opening them so that no sediment remains at the bottom&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt;An oil level that is too low and too high will impair the operation of the transmission&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Reinstall the level verification cap &lt;B&gt;B &lt;/B&gt;and tighten it to &lt;B&gt;45 Nm&lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt;Always replace the gasket of the level verification cap &lt;B&gt;B&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Reinstall the lower cover&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Lowering the vehicle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;/body&gt;  &lt;/html&gt;</Corpo>
